    "conventions": "Most Pakistanis are Muslim and carry Arabic, Persian or Turkic origin first names, often compound for men (Muhammad Usman, Ghulam Abbas). The last name is usually a family, clan or caste name (Butt, Malik, Chaudhry in Punjab; Siddiqui, Qureshi, Rizvi among Urdu speakers in Karachi; Khan, Yousafzai, Afridi among Pashtuns; Soomro, Memon, Jatoi in Sindh; Baloch, Rind, Bugti in Balochistan). Some people simply use their father's name, or a second given name, as a last name. Women often keep their father's family name or take the husband's after marriage. Friends shorten names (Mani, Bilu, Saadi) and add ji or bhai out of respect.",
